                <pb facs="0354" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg220"/>

                <head>No. 146.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 6,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Directs Mr. Denby to express to the Chinese Government the surprise and regret
                    with which the United States learn of obstruction being placed by Chinese
                    officials in the way of Corea’s diplomatic representation in the United States
                    as stipulated in existing treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
